{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SLdDpARhAys2pgouNUptf7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified by differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries, to stress-test a spec-driven AI code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: SRDs in `docs/specs/` are the source of truth. `cmd/<utility>/` holds per-utility Go implementations with differential tests. `pkg/sys/`, `pkg/format/`, `pkg/testutils/` provide shared infrastructure. The orchestrator drives Claude agents to generate code from SRDs.\n\n**Current state**: Several utilities are implemented (true, false, yes, basename, dirname, tee, head, sponge, du), and seq is nearly complete with only R4.4 remaining. The pkg/ infrastructure packages exist. Most utilities have specs but no code.\n\n**Current release**: rel02.2 has one remaining requirement (srd019-seq R4.4). After that, rel03.0 (wc) is the next full release to implement.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n1. **srd019-seq R4.4** (rel02.2) -- completes the release, only one requirement left\n2. **srd005-wc R1.1-R3.2** (rel03.0) -- next full release; 22 total requirements, first 12 fit in 3 tasks\n\n## Weight Budget Checks\n\n```\nTask 0: srd019-seq R4.4 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 1: srd005-wc R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1)\nTotal weight: 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 2: srd005-wc R2.1(w=1) + R2.2(w=1) + R2.3(w=1) + R2.4(w=1)\nTotal weight: 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 3: srd005-wc R2.5(w=1) + R2.6(w=1) + R3.1(w=1) + R3.2(w=1)\nTotal weight: 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n(Weights assumed default=1; requirements.yaml contents not in project_context.)\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/seq: remaining edge case (srd019-seq R4.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd019-seq.yaml (R4.4 requirement definition)\n      - cmd/seq/main.go (existing seq implementation to extend)\n      - cmd/seq/seq_test.go (existing differential tests to extend)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/seq/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Implement behavior specified by R4.4\n      - path: cmd/seq/seq_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases covering R4.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd019-seq R4.4 per the SRD specification, extending the existing cmd/seq implementation\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Follow the existing code patterns and structure in cmd/seq/main.go\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use testutils.BuildBinary and testutils.RunDiffTests with DiffTest structs for differential testing against the gseq reference binary\n      - id: D3\n        text: Set LC_ALL=C in the test Env field for locale-independent comparison\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: srd019-seq R4.4 behavior is implemented in cmd/seq/main.go\n      - id: AC2\n        text: Differential test cases for R4.4 are added to cmd/seq/seq_test.go\n      - id: AC3\n        text: go test ./cmd/seq/... -count=1 passes\n      - id: AC4\n        text: go vet ./cmd/seq/... reports no issues\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/wc: core counting and standard input (srd005-wc R1.1-R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd005-wc.yaml (R1.1-R1.4 requirement definitions)\n      - cmd/seq/main.go (reference for cmd/ package structure, flag parsing, and SIGPIPE handler)\n      - cmd/seq/seq_test.go (reference for differential test structure using testutils)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/wc/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: Initial wc implementation covering R1.1-R1.4 -- core counting logic and standard input handling\n      - path: cmd/wc/wc_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for R1.1-R1.4 against gwc reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd005-wc R1.1 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd005-wc R1.2 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd005-wc R1.3 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd005-wc R1.4 per the SRD specification\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main to match GNU coreutils SIGPIPE behavior\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\") to compile the Go binary and testutils.RunDiffTests to compare against the gwc reference binary\n      - id: D3\n        text: Call exec.LookPath(\"gwc\") and t.Skip if the reference binary is not found\n      - id: D4\n        text: Set LC_ALL=C in the test Env field for locale-independent comparison\n      - id: D5\n        text: Build the binary into bin/wc using \"go build -o bin/wc ./cmd/wc/\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/wc/main.go exists and compiles successfully\n      - id: AC2\n        text: srd005-wc R1.1 through R1.4 are implemented\n      - id: AC3\n        text: cmd/wc/wc_test.go contains differential tests covering R1.1-R1.4\n      - id: AC4\n        text: go test ./cmd/wc/... -count=1 passes\n      - id: AC5\n        text: go vet ./cmd/wc/... reports no issues\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/wc: flag selection and output formatting (srd005-wc R2.1-R2.4)\"\n  dependency: 1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd005-wc.yaml (R2.1-R2.4 requirement definitions)\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (existing wc implementation to extend)\n      - cmd/wc/wc_test.go (existing differential tests to extend)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/wc/main.go\n        action: modify\n        no